16:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-amber-200 text-gray-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Your task: "}],"Understand the pipeline that turns a documented visit into money in the practice's account, and where you sit in it."]}]
17:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"The job title joins two related but genuinely different roles. A medical coder reads the clinical documentation and translates what happened into standardized codes: a diagnosis code describing the patient's condition, and a procedure code describing what the provider did. A medical biller takes those codes, attaches the patient's insurance information, produces a claim, submits it to the payer, and pursues it until it is paid or properly resolved."}]
18:["$","p","2",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"In a large hospital these are separate departments. In a practice the size of Lakeside, one person often does both, which is why the training covers both. The skills differ: coding rewards precision, patience, and comfort with reference material. Billing rewards persistence, organization, and a willingness to make the follow-up phone call nobody else wants to make."}]
19:["$","div","3",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6","children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 mb-4","children":"Key terms"}],["$","dl",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Encounter"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"A single documented interaction between a patient and a provider. Every claim begins with one."}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Diagnosis code"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"A code describing the patient's condition — why care was needed. In the United States these come from ICD-10-CM."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Procedure code"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"A code describing what the provider did — the service delivered. These come from CPT and HCPCS Level II."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Claim"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"The formal request for payment sent to a payer, carrying the codes, the provider's identifiers, and the patient's coverage information."}]]}],["$","div","4",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Payer"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Whoever is being asked to pay — a commercial insurer, Medicare, Medicaid, or in some cases the patient directly."}]]}],["$","div","5",{"className":"sm:flex sm:gap-4","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-gray-900 sm:w-48 sm:flex-shrink-0","children":"Reimbursement"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"The payment a payer makes for a covered service, which is usually a contracted rate rather than the amount billed."}]]}]]}]]}]
1a:["$","div","1",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"The pipeline from visit to payment"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"The sequence below is the backbone of the entire field. Every later module in this program is a detailed treatment of one or two of these steps, so it is worth learning the shape of the whole thing before going deeper into any part of it."}],["$","figure","1",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Step"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"What happens"}],["$","th","2",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Who does it"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"1. Pre-registration"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Demographics and insurance are captured and verified before the visit"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Front desk"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"2. Eligibility and authorization"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Coverage is confirmed; prior authorization obtained if the payer requires it"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Front desk or billing"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"3. The encounter"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"The provider delivers and documents care"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Provider"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"4. Coding"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Documentation is translated into diagnosis and procedure codes"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Coder"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"5. Charge entry"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Codes and charges are entered into the practice management system"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Biller or coder"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"6. Claim scrubbing"}],"$L1f","$L20"]}],"$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25"]}]]}]}],"$L26"]}],"$L27"]}]]}]
1b:["$","div","2",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6","children":"Why accuracy is a compliance matter"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"It is tempting to think of coding as a revenue exercise where higher codes are better. That framing is both wrong and genuinely dangerous. A code is a factual assertion about what happened to a patient, submitted to a payer that may be a federal program. Submitting a code the documentation does not support is a false claim, and the consequences are not limited to the money being recouped."}],["$","figure","1",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Error"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"What it means"}],["$","th","2",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Consequence"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Upcoding"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Reporting a more complex or expensive service than was documented"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Overpayment recovery, penalties under the False Claims Act, exclusion from federal programs"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Undercoding"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Reporting a lower level of service than was documented"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Lost revenue, and a distorted record of the patient's care and the practice's case mix"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"The two ways coding goes wrong"}]]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Undercoding is sometimes treated as the safe error. It is not. It misrepresents the care delivered just as upcoding does, it starves the practice of revenue it legitimately earned, and a pattern of it can itself attract attention. The goal is never the highest code or the lowest code. It is the code the documentation supports."}],["$","div","3",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"The governing principle of this entire field is one sentence: if it was not documented, it was not done. A coder codes from the documentation, not from what they assume happened, not from what the provider says in the hallway, and not from what would pay better. When the documentation does not support a code, the correct action is to query the provider — never to code what you believe they meant."]}],["$","$L28","4",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"A provider tells you verbally that an office visit involved a detailed examination, but the note in the chart documents only a brief exam. What should you do?","options":["Code the higher level of service, since the provider confirmed what happened","Code from the documentation as written, and query the provider to amend the note if the exam was more extensive","Code the lower level and say nothing, since undercoding is always safe","Split the difference and code a mid-level visit"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Coders code from the documentation. If the record does not support the higher level, the fix is a provider query that gives the provider the opportunity to amend the note properly — not a coding decision that papers over the gap. If the note is amended appropriately, the higher code becomes supportable; if it is not amended, the documented level stands.","optionRationales":["A verbal statement is not documentation. Coding above what the record supports is upcoding, regardless of what you were told.","Correct. Code what is documented, and query the provider so the record can be corrected through the proper process if the care was genuinely more extensive.","Undercoding is not safe. It misrepresents the encounter and costs the practice revenue it legitimately earned, and doing it knowingly is its own problem.","There is no averaging in coding. The level of service is determined by what the documentation supports, not by compromise."]}}]]}]]}]
1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Trace a single encounter through the whole pipeline in writing, in your own words."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Invent a straightforward encounter: a patient with a sore throat sees a provider, who examines them and performs a rapid strep test. Write three sentences describing what happened clinically."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"For each of the eleven pipeline steps, write one sentence describing what happens to this specific encounter at that step. Where you do not yet know the detail, write what question you would need answered."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Identify the two steps in your list where you think an error would be most expensive to fix later, and explain why in a sentence each."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write down one question about this pipeline that you cannot yet answer. Keep the list — by the end of this program you should be able to answer it, and checking back is a good measure of your progress."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
